"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[63850],{863850:s=>{s.exports='# Assets Commands\n\nCommands for searching, discovering, and reading workspace assets via `runDatabricksPrivateCli`.\n\n## Recommended Workflow\n\nWhen the user asks about data, assets, or wants to explore the workspace, follow this order:\n\n1. **`assets for-you`** — Start here. Fetches the user\'s favorites, popular assets, and AI-suggested recommendations. Best for open-ended requests like "what data do I have?" or "show me something interesting."\n2. **`assets search`** — Use when you need keyword-based discovery. Search across multiple asset types (tables, dashboards, queries, notebooks, jobs, etc.).\n3. **`assets read`** — Read full details of a specific asset found via for-you or search results.\n\n**Decision tree:**\n\n- User has no specific query → `assets for-you`\n- User mentions a topic/keyword → `assets search <keyword>`\n- User wants their own assets → `assets search <keyword> --owner-only`\n- You have an asset ID from previous results → `assets read <type> <id>`\n\n## assets search\n\nSearch workspace assets by keyword. Returns results grouped by asset type.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\nassets search <query> [--types <csv>] [--limit <n>] [--sort-by <field>] [--owner-only] [--page-token <token>]\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n| Argument       | Required | Description                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<query>`      | Yes      | Keywords to search for (positional)                                                                                                                   |\n| `--types`      | No       | Comma-separated asset types: `tables`, `queries`, `notebooks`, `dashboards`, `pipelines`, `jobs`, `files`, `alerts`, `endpoints`, `models`, `folders` |\n| `--limit`      | No       | Number of results per asset type (max 5, default 3)                                                                                                   |\n| `--sort-by`    | No       | Sort order: `score`, `popularity`, `updated_at`, `name`                                                                                               |\n| `--owner-only` | No       | Restrict results to assets owned by the current user                                                                                                  |\n| `--page-token` | No       | Pagination token from a previous response                                                                                                             |\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```\nassets search my_table\nassets search revenue --types tables,notebooks --limit 5\nassets search etl_pipeline --sort-by popularity\nassets search dashboard --types dashboards --owner-only\nassets search ml_model --types models,endpoints\n```\n\n## assets for-you\n\nFetch personalized asset recommendations: favorites, popular, and suggested assets. **Use this as the first step** for data exploration requests.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\nassets for-you [--limit <n>] [--keywords <text>]\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n| Argument     | Required | Description                                     |\n| ------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `--limit`    | No       | Number of results per category (default 10)     |\n| `--keywords` | No       | Optional keywords for suggested asset filtering |\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```\nassets for-you\nassets for-you --limit 5\nassets for-you --keywords "sales dashboard"\n```\n\n## assets read\n\nRead an asset\'s details by type and ID.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\nassets read <assetType> <assetId>\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n| Argument      | Required | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<assetType>` | Yes      | Asset type: `notebook`, `query`, `file`, `folder`, `directory`, `pipeline`, `dashboard`, `dashboardDraft`, `job` |\n| `<assetId>`   | Yes      | Asset identifier (numeric ID, string ID, or workspace path for directories)                                      |\n\nAlternative flag syntax: `assets read --type notebook --id 12345`\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```\nassets read notebook 12345\nassets read query abc-def-123\nassets read dashboard 67890\nassets read job 98765\nassets read directory /Workspace/Users/user@example.com\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Always start with `assets for-you`** when the user hasn\'t specified a search query — it surfaces the most relevant assets without needing keywords.\n- Use `assets search` for keyword-based discovery across all asset types.\n- Use `--owner-only` on `assets search` to narrow results to the user\'s own assets.\n- Use `assets read` when you already know the asset type and ID (e.g., from a previous search result or user-provided link).\n- `directory` is an alias for `folder` — both work with `assets read`.\n- All commands return structured JSON responses.\n'}}]);
